# ★★★ BUILD OUTPUT AND SIGNING MATERIAL, BECAUSE THE PACKAGING SCRIPTS TELL YOU TO PUT IT HERE
# (2026-09-04, found while moving the macOS packaging lane into this tree). build_macos_ne_app.sh looks for
# app.provisionprofile and systemextension.provisionprofile in <tree>/var/

# ★ AND WHERE THE WINDOWS BUILD PUTS ITS OUTPUT (2026-09-04). build-msi.ps1 used to write two directories
# ABOVE this tree, which is the monorepo root here and somebody's home directory for a receiver who unpacked
# the tree on its own. It writes inside now, so this tree has to say the output is not source.
/outputs/signing — Apple credentials, issued
# to whoever builds this — and the packagers write their artifacts to <tree>/var. In the monorepo an outer
# .gitignore covered this path; that file does not travel with the published tree, so a receiver following the
# instructions would have had git track their own signing material.
/var/

# ★ AND WHERE THE WINDOWS BUILD PUTS ITS OUTPUT (2026-09-04). build-msi.ps1 used to write two directories
# ABOVE this tree, which is the monorepo root here and somebody's home directory for a receiver who unpacked
# the tree on its own. It writes inside now, so this tree has to say the output is not source.
/outputs/

# Built by `go build` in that directory; the published tree carries source, not binaries.
clients/windows-wfp/packaging/cmd/profileapply/profileapply
